      "notes": "Conditional coefficient parity compares K0 and K0_prime at the published printed precision, with adopted V0=154.5678863704812 A^3 per conventional Fe3C cell (Z=4) held fixed. Published K0=161 +/-2 GPa and K0_prime=5.9 +/-0.2 are retained unchanged. V0 is adopted from the published calculated full-range curve, not a printed source coefficient or the ambient measurement. Its uncertainty and the original fixed/free V0 convention are unrecovered. Numerical coefficient agreement does not establish uncertainty agreement, author-workflow reproduction or physical validation. The primary experimental dataset is all 19 numbered p1-p19 points from final Table S1, with published ruby pressures and reported widths, spanning 1.8-47.4 GPa at nominal 293 K. The recorded comparison uses equal pressure weights with V0 fixed and K0/K0_prime free. It gives K0=160.994011 +/-2.532193 GPa and K0_prime=5.919478 +/-0.240867, displayed as 161 +/-3 and 5.9 +/-0.2 at the paper precision. The K0 uncertainty is not reproduced: 2.532193 GPa rounds to 3, not the published 2 GPa. Covariance is inverse(J^T J)*SSE/(19-2), conditional on exact V0 and exact input volumes. Source coordinate widths are preserved but are not the weights in this comparison; source confidence and calibration covariance are unknown. The 22 digitized Figure 1 markers remain separate supplementary evidence, not the primary dataset. No ambient or p20-p22 point is added. For p16, the final source volume is 133.25 A^3, not the alternate SHELX cell 133.58 A^3. Published split fits remain audit-only. The main text rounds the upper limit to 47 GPa; Table S1 reaches 47.4 GPa. The nominal split ranges do not establish separate structural phases or a phase-stability envelope.",
